cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Carrying an ECG-AI threshold from inpatients to outpatients: a retrospective measurement of three structural heart disease models in one hospital system"
message: If you use this repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abbou
    given-names: Ruben
repository-code: https://github.com/rabbou/ecg-conformal-shift
# v1.0.0 and v1.1.0 are tags of earlier articles; this one is cited as 2.0.0, and
# date-released is written when that tag is made at the merge.
version: 2.0.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  At Columbia, a threshold set to catch 90% of inpatients with moderate or
  worse structural heart disease caught 71.6% of outpatients with
  it for a network trained on EchoNext, 72.7% for the published
  EchoNext mini-model and 71.6% for ECGFounder, while the AUROC
  moved from 0.815 to 0.805 for the trained network. Set
  again on 100 outpatients with known diagnoses, the threshold caught
  91.6% of the other outpatients' ill on average and flagged
  70 of 100 healthy; set on 858 separate outpatients, it
  caught 86.3%, 87.8% and 89.7%, short of 90% for
  all three models. An infarction
  model carried from PTB-XL to hospitals in Chongqing and Shandong is reported
  beside it, with a rotation of five public corpora on five rhythm and
  conduction diagnoses.
keywords:
  - electrocardiography
  - structural heart disease
  - decision threshold
  - sensitivity
  - spectrum effect
  - distribution shift
